---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Cloud Peptides collects, how it's used, and how to contact us about your data."
  lastUpdated="August 13, 2026"
>
  <p class="cp-policy-note">
    <strong>Note:</strong> Cloud Peptides is an operating name, not a claim about a specific registered
    business entity or jurisdiction. This policy describes our actual current data practices as plainly
    as we can.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud Peptides ("we," "us," "our") operates this website, which publishes cited research
    information about peptides and related compounds and sells research materials to verified
    researcher accounts. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:info.order.thecloud@proton.me"
      >info.order.thecloud@proton.me</a
    >
    or on <a href="https://discord.gg/8pF3AvHgT" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Discord</a
    >. We do not currently publish a physical mailing address.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect what's actually involved in operating this site today:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Researcher account information</strong> — accessing this site now requires creating a verified
      Independent Researcher account. Registration collects your full name, email address, password, country,
      state/province/region (when applicable), and research affiliation. We also record your affirmative
      acceptance of our Researcher Certification, Research Use Policy, Terms of Service, and Privacy Policy:
      which version of each you accepted, when, and whether your email was verified at that time. That
      acceptance record is kept permanently as part of your account's history and is never edited after
      the fact, even by us — a later re-acceptance (for example, if we materially update the certification)
      adds a new record rather than changing the old one. See our <a href="/research-use-policy"
        >Research Use Policy</a
      > for what the certification itself says.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Account status</strong> — whether your account is active or suspended, and, if suspended,
      that fact and the reason given. Administrative actions on accounts (registration, email verification,
      certification acceptance, suspension, reinstatement) are recorded in an internal, admin-only activity
      log.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — the name, email address, and message you submit are
      relayed directly to our inbox by email. We do not currently store contact form submissions in a
      database.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Order-request submissions</strong> — placing an order request collects your name, email
      address, phone number (optional), shipping address, and any notes you add, along with your confirmation
      that you are 18+ and accept our <a href="/shop-terms">Shop Terms</a>. Like contact
      submissions, an order request is relayed directly to our inbox by email (with a copy sent back
      to you as an acknowledgement) — we do not currently store order requests in a database, and
      submitting one does not take payment or create a binding sale.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anti-abuse/verification data</strong> — the contact form and the order-request form are
      protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a bot-detection challenge, and a short-lived cooldown cookie
      that prevents rapid resubmission from the same browser. Account registration and sign-in are protected
      by rate-limiting on our side.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Standard technical data</strong> — like any website, requests to this site pass through
      our hosting/security provider, Cloudflare, which processes technical information (such as IP address)
      to serve the site and to detect abuse (for example, our rate-limiting on forms and on sign-in).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference</strong> — if you switch to dark mode, that choice is saved in your browser's
      local storage on your device only; it is never sent to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shop cart contents</strong> — while browsing the shop, any items you add to a cart are held
      in your browser's local storage on your device only, not on our servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Administrative accounts</strong> — our editorial staff sign in through the same account
      system, with elevated internal permissions, to manage published research content and researcher
      accounts. Staff accounts are internal and are not created through public registration.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not currently operate a newsletter or advertising trackers, and we do not sell your
    personal information to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      To create and operate your researcher account, verify your email address, confirm your
      certification and eligibility to access the site, and — if needed — to suspend or reinstate an
      account or require you to reaffirm the certification.
    </li>
    <li>To respond to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website (for example, blocking spam and abuse).</li>
    <li>To review and respond to order requests and communicate with you about them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>This site sets a small number of cookies and browser-local-storage entries:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A session cookie that keeps you signed in once you've logged into your researcher account
      (this cookie is required — the site does not offer any content to signed-out visitors beyond
      the account-creation and legal pages).
    </li>
    <li>A short-lived cookie that enforces a brief cooldown between contact-form submissions.</li>
    <li>Your dark/light theme choice and shop cart contents, both stored only in your browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    That's the complete list — every one is strictly necessary for a feature you're actively using
    (spam prevention, staying signed in, remembering your theme/cart). We do not use analytics
    cookies, advertising or cross-site tracking cookies, or any other nonessential tracking
    technology, and have no plans to add any without updating this policy first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because every cookie here is strictly necessary rather than for tracking or analytics, we don't
    show a cookie-consent banner today. If that ever changes — for example, if we add analytics or
    advertising — we will revisit this decision and add proper consent controls before doing so, not
    after.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties we work with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, content delivery, security, and bot/abuse protection (Turnstile).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resend</strong> — delivers the emails generated by our contact and order-request forms.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts the database and authentication system that power our published
      research content, shop catalog, and researcher/staff accounts, and sends the email-verification
      and password-reset emails tied to your account.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each of these providers processes data only as needed to provide their respective service to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    Contact-form messages and order requests are retained in our email inbox until we delete them.
    We don't currently have a fixed automatic deletion schedule for that inbox — if you'd like a
    message you sent removed, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Researcher account information (profile details and account status) is retained for as long as
    your account exists. Certification-acceptance records are append-only by design — kept
    permanently as a compliance record even if your account is later suspended, and never edited
    after the fact — but the profile details tied to your account can still be corrected or deleted
    on request as described below.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    We don't yet offer a self-service page to view, correct, or export your own account profile
    directly. If you want to know what we hold about you, correct it, or have your account and
    profile information deleted, email us and we'll respond directly. Deleting your account will end
    your access to the site; it does not remove the append-only certification-acceptance history
    described above, which we keep as a compliance record of what was agreed to and when.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed to anyone under 18. Registration requires an affirmative confirmation
    that you are 18 or older, and we do not knowingly create accounts for, or otherwise collect
    personal information from, anyone under that age.
  </p>

  <h2>International visitors</h2>
  <p>
    We have not yet implemented a specific regional privacy-compliance program (for example, GDPR or
    CCPA-specific processes). If that changes, we will update this policy to describe it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this page as our practices change. The date at the top reflects the most recent
    update.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:info.order.thecloud@proton.me"
      >info.order.thecloud@proton.me</a
    >
    or through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
